{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum","id":1340817,"title":"Immortals in Trinity Continuum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-11T11:51:54-07:00","id":1340817,"title":"Immortals in Trinity Continuum","content":"So I really love the concept of the immortal, the undying, and such. Now normally I go with using versions somewhat modified from the toolkits that are both World and Chronicles of Darkness, with some lightening one might say. I also sometimes use the idea of the True Immortal and the Lodge of the Undying from the decades old book Witchcraft by CJ Carella. <br /> <br /> But I was thinking about it recently and there is nothing that says living immortals can't exist in the Trinity Continuum. Heck, theoretically, if a Psiad appeared millennia ago all they would need is one point in VK and would have no effective lifespan, making them immortal. But I was also thinking of other ways to go about such a thing. An example is something like a natural born Superior (mechanically that is, thematically they would be something else) whose mastery of physical attributes would lead to immorality. <br /> <br /> But yeah I think it would be a fascinating question to ask - what a immortal campaign set in the Trinity Continuum would look like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T13:53:35-07:00","id":1340836,"title":"","content":"My home game has several immortals. Back in 1e I ran a series of interconnected games across all three titles. Several NPCs were alive in all three eras. I never had a player play a character that popped up in more than one era, but some of those characters became NPCs in other eras (the players were no longer available). If you have the player characters existing across eras that will likely lead to very powerful characters by the Aeon era. I think the system allows for it, and now that the rules are more harmonious that 1e I suspect it wouldn't be too much of a hastle.<br /> <br /> If you want immortal PCs across eras without them getting too OP consider rebuilding for each era. They should start with bonus XP, but there is no need to actuall give them the nigh infinite XP the character would have had it actually been played for over a century. Just chalk it up to the character having forgotten some things along the way, or slacked off on their training for a couple decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T16:42:22-07:00","id":1340866,"title":"","content":"I keep seeing this on the threads, and I don't know where it's coming from: Why does everyone think that knowing Vitakinesis grants you immortality? What is that based on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4009-wynterknight","name":"Wynterknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T16:57:28-07:00","id":1340868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wynterknight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1340866#post1340866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep seeing this on the threads, and I don't know where it's coming from: Why does everyone think that knowing Vitakinesis grants you immortality? What is that based on?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Page 260 in Aeon Core in the sidebar Psionic Longevity. &quot;Vitakinetics and biokinetics with high latency or who have learned to enhance their powers all seem to have ceased aging and may well be immortal,and this also appears to be true for anyone with a Vitakinetic Auxiliary Mode.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T17:04:11-07:00","id":1340869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1340836#post1340836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My home game has several immortals. Back in 1e I ran a series of interconnected games across all three titles. Several NPCs were alive in all three eras. I never had a player play a character that popped up in more than one era, but some of those characters became NPCs in other eras (the players were no longer available). If you have the player characters existing across eras that will likely lead to very powerful characters by the Aeon era. I think the system allows for it, and now that the rules are more harmonious that 1e I suspect it wouldn't be too much of a hastle.<br /> <br /> If you want immortal PCs across eras without them getting too OP consider rebuilding for each era. They should start with bonus XP, but there is no need to actuall give them the nigh infinite XP the character would have had it actually been played for over a century. Just chalk it up to the character having forgotten some things along the way, or slacked off on their training for a couple decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of having a set of people occassionally return to new games because technically they would still be a live is brilliant and fun. So thumbs up on that. <br /> <br /> On the whole experience one part of me is like &quot;it makes sense that when not on adventure one's experience flow is slower&quot; but then another part of me is like &quot;but but but why should my century plus year old person be low level!!!&quot; hehe<br /> <br /> When it comes to the power groups of Psiads and Novas I do really think it would be hard for there to be a millennia old Nova just sitting around without anyone knowing about it, at least under current rules. (I could see Quantum maximums and experience costs being greater in periods of low quantum energy in the environment as a balance point, that and a focus more on Mega-Edges than straight up powers). But I could see Psiads existing as there powers, while definitely mighty are a bit more, or at least can be, lowkey. <br /> <br /> If one were to use the Superior rules (but change the fluff description about it) then one could probably get something like the Immortals from Highlander. hehe <br /> <br /> It would be cool to have a book about Inspired through the centuries. I think it would be fun to be a Psiad born in the ancient past who has lived and developed all these years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-11T19:24:13-07:00","id":1340889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1340868#post1340868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Page 260 in Aeon Core in the sidebar Psionic Longevity. &amp;quot;Vitakinetics and biokinetics with high latency or who have learned to enhance their powers all seem to have ceased aging and may well be immortal,and this also appears to be true for anyone with a Vitakinetic Auxiliary Mode.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want immortals, this is a quick and easy way to justify them. (For psionicists, at least.)<br /> <br /> But, this is based on less than 20 years of data* and may not be true. <br /> <br /> *Bhurano may or may not be special in this regard, and other hundreds+ year old psiads haven\u2019t made themselves known, if any are out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T12:08:56-07:00","id":1340981,"title":"","content":"The solution to 1k+ novas and why there's so few psiads etc is every so often they feel a call to come together to fight.. the last one standing gains all the psy/quantum of the others immediatly transcending beyond the human condition...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T21:04:51-07:00","id":1341046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1340981#post1340981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The solution to 1k+ novas and why there's so few psiads etc is every so often they feel a call to come together to fight.. the last one standing gains all the psy/quantum of the others immediatly transcending beyond the human condition...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see what you did there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T21:28:42-07:00","id":1341049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1340981#post1340981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The solution to 1k+ novas and why there's so few psiads etc is every so often they feel a call to come together to fight.. the last one standing gains all the psy/quantum of the others immediatly transcending beyond the human condition...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just... NEVER... put aliens in this story... you will latter have to retcon it... it will be a total disaster...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-12T22:55:37-07:00","id":1341057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1341049#post1341049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Just... NEVER... put aliens in this story... you will latter have to retcon it... it will be a total disaster...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't know... I mean who wouldn't want to play an Immortal going around murdering Doyen for quick... I mean psi points.<br /> <br /> <br /> ... I mean I started this as a joke but the more I think about how well Highlander might work better in the TC than the traditional attempt to tie it some version of the World of Darkness...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 10-13-2019, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T09:21:12-07:00","id":1341097,"title":"","content":"The whole putting Highlander Immortals in Trinity Continuum works pretty well. I mean Flux could be Quickening. I could also see using the Superior template to represent the special abilities that the Immortals have access to. But even more using it in TC rather than WoD/CoD means there is no need to darken the world and the splat. <br /> <br /> Which is another reason why I think there being some sort of immortal group hanging around in TC would be very cool. Said immortal group would have various paranormal things to handle but won't have to worry about sharing the dark world with multiple monstrous groups.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think it would be really cool to run a TC game that moves through the ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T09:38:31-07:00","id":1341100,"title":"","content":"I would put the Immortals (as Highlander) as Talents, no powers other than Gifts and Inspiration (they call it Quickening), except for 2 specific traits, the character never dies when taken out, unless if the head is taken of, and they can detect other inspired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T09:42:22-07:00","id":1341101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1341100#post1341100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would put the Immortals (as Highlander) as Talents, no powers other than Gifts and Inspiration (they call it Quickening), except for 2 specific traits, the character never dies when taken out, unless if the head is taken of, and they can detect other inspired.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Talents could totally work for them it might be more fun to have the members of the Watchers be Talents and the actual Immortals be Superiors. I say this because we clearly see through the times of the TV show that the Immortals have some sort of special abilities. Ones which could be mechanically described using Superior rules. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I love options","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T14:54:53-07:00","id":1341149,"title":"","content":"I know what you mean about the immortals, they do some fantastic stuff in the series, more than in the movies, indeed they look really Superhuman in essence. My opinion now:<br /> <br /> Talents can do quite fantastic stuff to by spending inspiration and having enough of the proper facet. Let\u2019s say a talent can hold the stone door open a little longer if spend inspiration on a Reflective action, or cause more damage to a building or a vehicle if have enough destructive. Talents can also increase their scale by 1 for a single action by spending Inspiration<u>.</u>And I didn\u2019t even touch the gifts that can be very flexible.<br /> <br /> The weak point in talents is not what they can do, as they are extremely flexible, but how often they can do amazing things. If it\u2019s a thing they do once in a while and the character get tired (uninspired) it can be a talent even if it seams really Superhuman. That\u2019s why I see Batman as a talent (likely Inspiration 8+) and not a dark star, his power is knowing the script of the story before it happens, basically dramatic editing, and a huge amount of skill, edges and gifts. same thing about the immortals, they do crazy stuff but not all the time, and they usually do lots of different stuff, not always the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T16:49:47-07:00","id":1341175,"title":"","content":"Yes, exactly. Honestly, when I think of Highlander its the show, its Duncan and Methos and the ethos of the Watchers we learn about there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I agree with you on the fact that Talents are quite powerful. But the fact that their powers are powered by both Momentum and Inspiration means they can't be used that often. Superior powers are basically if you have it then you can use it, which seems to be more inline with what Highlander Immortals (which are not automatically what I want when I think of Immortals in TC) look like. <br /> <br /> On Batman, honestly, yes, I think him as a Talent makes a lot of sense. Give him the Talent Gift to deal with beings with higher sclae and a vast assortment of Luck, Aptitutde Gifts and you get his ability,. That and his Inspired gadgets, which while not as say vast as a quantum powered one can still do more things in smaller packages then other people can have access to. <br /> <br /> I guess one of the things about playing in an Immortal campaign is what one wants the players to be able to do. If you want clearly visible super powers then go with immortal Psiads or Novas, but if you want lowkey but clearly present and always able to be one step ahead of others then I think something like a Superior might work on a mechanical basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-13T18:27:16-07:00","id":1341191,"title":"","content":"What if something had a natural flux reserve though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T11:33:15-07:00","id":1341287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1341191#post1341191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if something had a natural flux reserve though?</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T16:10:24-07:00","id":1341338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1341287#post1341287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you mean by this?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A Talent who doesn't run out of inspiration. They seem to regenerate it at a reasonable interval?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T16:28:21-07:00","id":1341340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1341338#post1341338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Talent who doesn't run out of inspiration. They seem to regenerate it at a reasonable interval?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Well that would be really cool. It would mean that they would be able to use their powers quite a lot. Which would be cool. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> As an aside when one thinks about how humanity basically created their own power group - the Superiors - using science there is definitely the potential for other metanormal types to exist within the cosmology of TC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T18:01:13-07:00","id":1341359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1341340#post1341340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah. Well that would be really cool. It would mean that they would be able to use their powers quite a lot. Which would be cool.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So my Inkling for my Immortal idea which I will shamelessly from here call &quot;Princes of the Universe&quot;<br /> <br /> They are on the Flux/Paramorph/Talent Track.<br /> <br /> They have honest to Goodness Immortality: There are ways to put them down(Especially by eachother) but for the most part they end up getting up after 500 years in a cave annoyed...<br /> <br /> They Regenerate Inspiration faster than one dot a scene. I am not sure if once a round is too quick though.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T21:01:42-07:00","id":1341394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1341359#post1341359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They Regenerate Inspiration faster than one dot a scene. I am not sure if once a round is too quick though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe go with some sort of roll at the start of each scene, with them gaining bonus Inspiration equal to successes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T21:20:35-07:00","id":1341397,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that there are two directions one could go with high-powered Talents: <br /> <br /> \u2022 Play up the timeline manipulation and give them conscious probability manipulation, time travel, or dimension hopping abilities. <br /> <br /> \u2022 amp up their Gifts, especially the ones related to attributes and skills. <br /> <br /> The latter option gets into similar conceptual territory as Exalted: channel an empowering energy (Essence in Exalted; parachronic Flux in TC) to enhance your competence and pull off stunts that range from extraordinary to flat-out impossible.<br /> <br /> You could even do both, with higher-level Gifts being the TC counterpart to Charm Trees (or whatever Exalted calls them) and the conscious parachronic powers being the TC counterpart to Exalted's Sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-15-2019, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T03:02:31-07:00","id":1341419,"title":"","content":"If you think Stalwarts can only control their body and Novas can control the entire universe, the possibilities for Talents are far more versatile. I have been working on my Techniques (for Excelsiors, the next step on Talents) and it\u2019s going back and forward on how it works, but I try to give total flexibility on the effects, bolts of pure inspiration, mist control, summoning trans dimensional creatures, things like that, and of course speed, time control and lucky (lucky is more like a basic power for probability control).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T11:08:24-07:00","id":1341657,"title":"","content":"I would absolutely love, LOVE, to see something like the charms of the Solar Exalted in the Trinity Continuum setting. Amusingly enough the game mechanics would support such high powered characters, which is one of the difficulties that might occur. <br /> <br /> But yeah Talents with more supernal level Aptitude and Luck Gifts would be incredibly fun. As would them being able to unlock and gain more dimensional powers. <br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> While Superiors are limited to only controlling themselves I do not see Stalwarts having any similar limitation, as they are proto-novas in some ways. <br /> <br /> The thing I was saying is that if one considers the source of immortality being an internal thing it makes perfect sense for True Immortals to basically only have powers that effect the self, since it is the self they master. If one was to use that idea then I could see using the mechanics (but again not the fluff) for Superiors, just with some additions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T11:19:36-07:00","id":1341660,"title":"","content":"In 1e, all the Stalwart powers were about the control of themselves and their body (it include sensing powers, and shapechanging), no quantum blast or similar, much like Superior powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T11:29:17-07:00","id":1341663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1341660#post1341660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e, all the Stalwart powers were about the control of themselves and their body (it include sensing powers, and shapechanging), no quantum blast or similar, much like Superior powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, lol. My bad. For some reason I had thought there was more world effecting abilities there. But I just checked and yeah everything is about the self (which, as you said, includes sensing powers which makes perfect sense to me). I like that dynamics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T12:33:17-07:00","id":1341681,"title":"","content":"My idea is that they scale their craziness.. or the world in someway naturally covers up for them. Like normal people can't just hide a sword in their trenchcoat and call it good. When two of them fight to the death crazy shit happens.. but they take all their flux with them when they quicken thus why there's not huge places of Flux all over the world when they fight.<br /> <br /> I Like the idea that they can get to exalt levels when they fight novas but could be 5000 yearold as a starting Tier 3 player...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T11:13:05-07:00","id":1342756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1340981#post1340981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The solution to 1k+ novas and why there's so few psiads etc is every so often they feel a call to come together to fight.. the last one standing gains all the psy/quantum of the others immediatly transcending beyond the human condition...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So there can be only one .... ?I couldn't resist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T12:59:58-07:00","id":1342783,"title":"","content":"There is no way, absolutely no way, to talk about Immortals and not state the iconic lines and such from Highlander. No way. hehe<br /> <br /> Thinking about it a bit more I can't help but think on how cool it would be to have a book or so with extremely powered up Talent Gifts. The fact that there abilities are based on Attribute and Skills (and Luck, but mostly the other two) gives so much potential design space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T16:27:45-07:00","id":1342830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1342756#post1342756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So there can be only one .... ?I couldn't resist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I mean.. that was litterally the joke I was going for before I noticed how well it would work in setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T04:57:40-08:00","id":1349049,"title":"","content":"One thing to consider about Highlander Immortals is the Quickening. When one of them is beheaded there;s a definite energy release that another Immortal can absorb. I'd figure that absorbing that energy immediately refills an Immortal's Inspiration pool and also gives them XP equal to the dead Immortal's Inspiration. Of course that situation might become a little problematic in a mixed game since other character types don't have such a quick XP gain potential. And even in a group of Immortals in tends to favor those who are specifically melee combat oriented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T19:54:21-08:00","id":1349250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349049#post1349049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to consider about Highlander Immortals is the Quickening. When one of them is beheaded there;s a definite energy release that another Immortal can absorb. I'd figure that absorbing that energy immediately refills an Immortal's Inspiration pool and also gives them XP equal to the dead Immortal's Inspiration. Of course that situation might become a little problematic in a mixed game since other character types don't have such a quick XP gain potential. And even in a group of Immortals in tends to favor those who are specifically melee combat oriented.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly my idea would be that the Quickening is just Immortal Diab. Its not something that happens often. That the Gathering is the real times of Murderation which is pretty much an &quot;Every inspired for themselves&quot; period and a quick path to godhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T20:31:45-08:00","id":1349257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349250#post1349250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly my idea would be that the Quickening is just Immortal Diab. Its not something that happens often. That the Gathering is the real times of Murderation which is pretty much an &quot;Every inspired for themselves&quot; period and a quick path to godhood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get the &quot;Diab&quot; reference. That said, pulling from <i>Highlander: The Series</i>, the larger portion of the episodes have Duncan engaging in some conflict with another Immortal that ends with guest-star Immortal losing his head. Cue lightning, property damage and Duncan getting just a little bit better at stuff. <br /> <br /> Consider how secret/known Immortals would be. As of the 2100s, the Aeon Trinity knows about Psiads. And Psiads are pretty much purpose-built with the ability to conceal themselves. The dude who looks the same in 1920 as he does in 2120 is going to be on Aeon's radar - especially if he leaves a trail of severed heads and electrical damage in his wake.<br /> <br /> It's one of the things I've considered in terms of my &quot;Paraquantum&quot; campaign. Part of the way I resolved it is to figure that Externals and their agents have been active to varying degree on Earth for a very, very long time. They predate Max Mercer by a lot. There are absolutely External agents in the Psi Orders, Aeon Trinity, FSA and pretty much any decent-sized or influential organization/nation/etc you can imagine. They're alien to our understand, but they greatly understand us. Much like a farmer understands his chickens and has no problem taking their eggs/potential children or butchering a couple to make a chicken dinner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T21:30:10-08:00","id":1349273,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Diablerie_(VTM\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Diablerie_(VTM</a>)<br /> <br /> Diablerie. It\u2019s a Vampire thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T08:05:28-08:00","id":1349341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349273#post1349273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Diablerie_(VTM\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Diablerie_(VTM</a>)<br /> <br /> Diablerie. It\u2019s a Vampire thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that now. But figure there's two big differences. First, Diablerie is taboo among vampire and results in execution if caught. It also shows up in a vamp's aura or blood. Finally it has a specific detrimental effect of reducing Humanity. The Quickening is fully acceptable among Immortals, who generally loners without a society or organization like the Camarilla, Sabbat etc.<br /> <br /> Second since Immortals can only die in a fairly specific way (severing the head) many normal dangers are kind of irrelevant to them. Perhaps a big enough weapon or attack might reduce them to atoms (which removes the head by definition), but for the most part an Immortal would only be in real danger from someone who was aware of the requirement to remove their head and had the means to do so. The most likely candidate for that would be another Immortal who was carrying a sword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T12:31:03-08:00","id":1349403,"title":"","content":"If you read the new Aeon book, they point out that Psions with Vitakinetic Modes and a high level of PSI don't age. This means that PCs from an Aeon campaign could be alive in a far future campaign. Similarly Novas, if low taint, can last for millennia. Does any of this help?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T12:33:38-08:00","id":1349405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349403#post1349403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you read the new Aeon book, they point out that Psions with Vitakinetic Modes and a high level of PSI don't age. This means that PCs from an Aeon campaign could be alive in a far future campaign. Similarly Novas, if low taint, can last for millennia. Does any of this help?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was actually what started me on this path. The fact that a psiad from say a few thousand years with even 1 dot in VK could be alive in the 21st century is all kinds of interesting. But even more I wouldn't be surprised if certain similar longevity existed for Novas, and the other Inspired including Talents and Superiors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T12:40:49-08:00","id":1349410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349403#post1349403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you read the new Aeon book, they point out that Psions with Vitakinetic Modes and a high level of PSI don't age. This means that PCs from an Aeon campaign could be alive in a far future campaign. Similarly Novas, if low taint, can last for millennia. Does any of this help?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Technically, it says they don't appear to age, but they also only have a few decades of evidence to support that. However, if you throw in a certain proxy, then maybe that's why she's lived so long?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T12:44:53-08:00","id":1349412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349403#post1349403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you read the new Aeon book, they point out that Psions with Vitakinetic Modes and a high level of PSI don't age. This means that PCs from an Aeon campaign could be alive in a far future campaign. Similarly Novas, if low taint, can last for millennia. Does any of this help?</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s an in-character quote, and as Florin says, there\u2019s only limited evidence to back it up. How true it is - or not - on the long-term scale is up to individual groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T12:46:33-08:00","id":1349414,"title":"","content":"Um with utmost respect I am going to turn into a five year old and plug my ears and go &quot;nah na nana can't hear you&quot; when you say it might not be true! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T12:50:53-08:00","id":1349416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349414#post1349414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um with utmost respect I am going to turn into a five year old and plug my ears and go &amp;quot;nah na nana can't hear you&amp;quot; when you say it might not be true! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I clearly said it\u2019s up to individual groups. If it\u2019s true at your table, it\u2019s true. If another table doesn\u2019t want immortal psions running around, it\u2019s not true.<br /> <br /> Under current evidence, it\u2019s just as possible that Vitakinetics just age really slowly and it can\u2019t be seen in 20 years of looking. Or they may not age at all, but once their allotted lifespan is up, they just put their affairs in order and die. <br /> <br /> Depends what you need for your part of the Continuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T19:16:04-08:00","id":1349487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349341#post1349341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get that now. But figure there's two big differences. First, Diablerie is taboo among vampire and results in execution if caught. It also shows up in a vamp's aura or blood. Finally it has a specific detrimental effect of reducing Humanity. The Quickening is fully acceptable among Immortals, who generally loners without a society or organization like the Camarilla, Sabbat etc.<br /> <br /> Second since Immortals can only die in a fairly specific way (severing the head) many normal dangers are kind of irrelevant to them. Perhaps a big enough weapon or attack might reduce them to atoms (which removes the head by definition), but for the most part an Immortal would only be in real danger from someone who was aware of the requirement to remove their head and had the means to do so. The most likely candidate for that would be another Immortal who was carrying a sword.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think that Immortal society is particularly gung ho about self murder, but rather there's sort of a Gathering/Gehenna mechanic that resets them every so often. That your immortals might have friends and not seriously murder eachother except when the Gathering comes and everyone sort of goes into full murder mode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T20:37:12-08:00","id":1349495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349487#post1349487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't think that Immortal society is particularly gung ho about self murder, but rather there's sort of a Gathering/Gehenna mechanic that resets them every so often. That your immortals might have friends and not seriously murder eachother except when the Gathering comes and everyone sort of goes into full murder mode.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm mostly coming at this from <i>Highlander: The Series</i>. That series showed Immortals in a fairly normal situation and not the Gathering/Gehenna/etc. Still, the world of Immortals as presented showed that if one Immortal had a problem with another one that they couldn't talk out, they pulled the slashing weapon of their choices and went at it until one of them was missing a head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T21:27:44-08:00","id":1349497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349049#post1349049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to consider about Highlander Immortals is the Quickening. When one of them is beheaded there;s a definite energy release that another Immortal can absorb. I'd figure that absorbing that energy immediately refills an Immortal's Inspiration pool and also gives them XP equal to the dead Immortal's Inspiration. Of course that situation might become a little problematic in a mixed game since other character types don't have such a quick XP gain potential. And even in a group of Immortals in tends to favor those who are specifically melee combat oriented.</div> </div> </div> </div>To avoid the XP problem, you could argue that gaining Quickening doesn't actually grant you any XP, it just allows you to immediately spend accumulated XP on various Immortal only traits. Without a Quickening, you instead have to spend some downtime training up your Immortal traits.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T05:49:48-08:00","id":1349552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349495#post1349495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm mostly coming at this from <i>Highlander: The Series</i>. That series showed Immortals in a fairly normal situation and not the Gathering/Gehenna/etc. Still, the world of Immortals as presented showed that if one Immortal had a problem with another one that they couldn't talk out, they pulled the slashing weapon of their choices and went at it until one of them was missing a head.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The series happens during The Gathering. They changed the narration at the opening in the 7th episode to clarify that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T05:50:43-08:00","id":1349553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349497#post1349497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To avoid the XP problem, you could argue that gaining Quickening doesn't actually grant you any XP, it just allows you to immediately spend accumulated XP on various Immortal only traits. Without a Quickening, you instead have to spend some downtime training up your Immortal traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might work (though figure that killing another Immortal would likely be something that occurs at the end of a scenario/chronicle anyway). I'd add that before fighting an Immortal the player can immediately define &quot;Killing this Immortal&quot; as a short-term Aspiration and a get an extra point of XP that way. I mean, fighting another Immortal is one of the few ways that an Immortal puts himself in real danger of death. It should be a pretty big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T06:13:17-08:00","id":1349566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349495#post1349495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm mostly coming at this from <i>Highlander: The Series</i>. That series showed Immortals in a fairly normal situation and not the Gathering/Gehenna/etc. Still, the world of Immortals as presented showed that if one Immortal had a problem with another one that they couldn't talk out, they pulled the slashing weapon of their choices and went at it until one of them was missing a head.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The first Episode of Highlander the series is &quot;The Gathering&quot; its pretty explicit that the Gathering was going on during the series. My idea would be Gatherings are sort of the inversion of the various major points(Hammersmith/Galatia etc), where the great chaos of flux is cleaned up in a decapitation event. For the most part this isn't the standard situation.<br /> <br /> That way you don't have to assume someone has lived 500 years killing 1 person every 2 or 3 weeks...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T08:06:19-08:00","id":1349590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349566#post1349566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My idea would be Gatherings are sort of the inversion of the various major points(Hammersmith/Galatia etc), where the great chaos of flux is cleaned up in a decapitation event. For the most part this isn't the standard situation.<br /> <br /> That way you don't have to assume someone has lived 500 years killing 1 person every 2 or 3 weeks...</div> </div> </div> </div>And instead of XP, Quickening can be a Flux event which refreshes your Inspiration pool. Trinity doesn't have things like Arcane beats, but you could add Inspiration XP which could only be used on Facets and Gifts. Then taking a head might get you 1 Inspiration XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T13:24:19-08:00","id":1349663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349566#post1349566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The first Episode of Highlander the series is &quot;The Gathering&quot; its pretty explicit that the Gathering was going on during the series. My idea would be Gatherings are sort of the inversion of the various major points(Hammersmith/Galatia etc), where the great chaos of flux is cleaned up in a decapitation event. For the most part this isn't the standard situation.<br /> <br /> That way you don't have to assume someone has lived 500 years killing 1 person every 2 or 3 weeks...</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. All I can say is that after that first episode, I don't recall The Gathering being mentioned again. And while it did seem to be a little less frequent as the series went on, most of the episode could be summed up as: Guest Immortal shows up. Duncan and Guest Immortal have a problem with each other. Duncan beheads Guest Immortal.<br /> <br /> At the same time, anyone using these character types in their game is free to do it however they want. If Immortals settle conflicts on holy ground by playing really intense games of tiddlywinks in your campaign, that's fine. <br /> <br /> For my part, I don't plan to include them in my game because I think they'd come off as a bit silly in the wake of Chromatics launching attacks, a pack of alien genetic rapists on their way and the corrupted pack of Mad Gods coming for us (not to mention all the stuff with the Externals). Also, a bunch of folks are chopping off each others' head and triggering mild electrical property damage doesn't seem especially concerning. At least that particular take on Immortals would come off as silly. There will be beings in my game that are immortal in terms of not aging. There might be beings that are immortal in terms of being both not aging and really, really difficult to kill, but swiping directly from <i>Highlander</i> just wouldn't work for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T17:03:05-08:00","id":1349728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349663#post1349663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe. All I can say is that after that first episode, I don't recall The Gathering being mentioned again. And while it did seem to be a little less frequent as the series went on, most of the episode could be summed up as: Guest Immortal shows up. Duncan and Guest Immortal have a problem with each other. Duncan beheads Guest Immortal.<br /> <br /> At the same time, anyone using these character types in their game is free to do it however they want. If Immortals settle conflicts on holy ground by playing really intense games of tiddlywinks in your campaign, that's fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Duncan spends most of his 400 years of life.. occasionally chatting up with immortals and occasionally getting into fights but they get away. Its the period of time between episode 1 and whenever in made for Tv movies that he actually murders the vast majority of his kills. The first episode calls it the beginning of the Gathering.<br /> <br /> The Gathering gives a Watsonian explanation for the Doyalistic of &quot;it would be boring if Ducan killed people off screen&quot;. And it gives a justification in a game for why you can have a relatively ancient starting character, without assuming they've been litterally fighting for their life every week for centuries.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For my part, I don't plan to include them in my game because I think they'd come off as a bit silly in the wake of Chromatics launching attacks, a pack of alien genetic rapists on their way and the corrupted pack of Mad Gods coming for us (not to mention all the stuff with the Externals). Also, a bunch of folks are chopping off each others' head and triggering mild electrical property damage doesn't seem especially concerning. At least that particular take on Immortals would come off as silly. There will be beings in my game that are immortal in terms of not aging. There might be beings that are immortal in terms of being both not aging and really, really difficult to kill, but swiping directly from <i>Highlander</i> just wouldn't work for me. </div> </div> </div>Compare it more to situations in the Trinity Core or Adventure! period vs say The most extreme ends of Aeon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T17:56:15-08:00","id":1349741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349728#post1349728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Duncan spends most of his 400 years of life.. occasionally chatting up with immortals and occasionally getting into fights but they get away. Its the period of time between episode 1 and whenever in made for Tv movies that he actually murders the vast majority of his kills. The first episode calls it the beginning of the Gathering.<br /> <br /> The Gathering gives a Watsonian explanation for the Doyalistic of &quot;it would be boring if Ducan killed people off screen&quot;. And it gives a justification in a game for why you can have a relatively ancient starting character, without assuming they've been litterally fighting for their life every week for centuries.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Compare it more to situations in the Trinity Core or Adventure! period vs say The most extreme ends of Aeon.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as Duncan goes, that's fine. I suspect that the large majority of people familiar with Highlander who participate in your will expect your game to reflect Highlander and Highlander: The Series in terms of decapitations.<br /> <br /> And my campaign is going to be taking place in the most extreme ends of Aeon - at least eventually. Sure in Core or Adventure, I could see and Immortal or two with a Psiad and maybe another Talent going around dealing with The Gathering and that would be a big deal. The winner of The Prize will become some kind of superbeing, maybe even on the level of a Tier III or Tier IV Nova. You need to make sure the One isn't going to be some kind of evil tyrant. In the regular Aeon the universe already has quite a few Tier IV Novas who are functionally lunatic gods. Also, in my game aside from all that, my players are going to need to stop an Extent cult from summoning Our Lady of Wounds, a potentially Tier V threat into Montressor Hospital.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T09:05:45-08:00","id":1349865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349741#post1349741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as Duncan goes, that's fine. I suspect that the large majority of people familiar with Highlander who participate in your will expect your game to reflect Highlander and Highlander: The Series in terms of decapitations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I would set it in some sort of Gathering level. I'm also not sure I'd 1 for 1 make them Highlander immortals in the Continuum but include Highlander Immortals as part of my thematic inspiration<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And my campaign is going to be taking place in the most extreme ends of Aeon - at least eventually. Sure in Core or Adventure, I could see and Immortal or two with a Psiad and maybe another Talent going around dealing with The Gathering and that would be a big deal. The winner of The Prize will become some kind of superbeing, maybe even on the level of a Tier III or Tier IV Nova. You need to make sure the One isn't going to be some kind of evil tyrant. In the regular Aeon the universe already has quite a few Tier IV Novas who are functionally lunatic gods. Also, in my game aside from all that, my players are going to need to stop an Extent cult from summoning Our Lady of Wounds, a potentially Tier V threat into Montressor Hospital. </div> </div> </div>Which is your choice. I just thought it was a weird thing to bring up. The Continuum contains fighting Space god Novas and low key James Bond and everything in between.<br /> <br /> However my Theoretical &quot;Prince of the Universe&quot; template wouldn't be merely beholden to lower tier timelines. The idea would be to go from having the occasional hidden sword fight between Immortals to as the world gets more crazy having full on Anime/Wuxia level powers.(These may be gated by Gatherings).<br /> <br /> I am not sure if throwing all my ideas in one basket is the best way of doing it ultimately and maybe just making Immortals another type of Exomorph variant might be the best for a highlander situation, but I also want a sort of Time Lord/Exalt for the Tier 3 Paramorph setup....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T10:00:35-08:00","id":1349876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349865#post1349865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is why I would set it in some sort of Gathering level. I'm also not sure I'd 1 for 1 make them Highlander immortals in the Continuum but include Highlander Immortals as part of my thematic inspiration<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Which is your choice. I just thought it was a weird thing to bring up. The Continuum contains fighting Space god Novas and low key James Bond and everything in between.<br /> <br /> However my Theoretical &quot;Prince of the Universe&quot; template wouldn't be merely beholden to lower tier timelines. The idea would be to go from having the occasional hidden sword fight between Immortals to as the world gets more crazy having full on Anime/Wuxia level powers.(These may be gated by Gatherings).<br /> <br /> I am not sure if throwing all my ideas in one basket is the best way of doing it ultimately and maybe just making Immortals another type of Exomorph variant might be the best for a highlander situation, but I also want a sort of Time Lord/Exalt for the Tier 3 Paramorph setup....</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of power/Tier, based on my observations, Immortals are pretty firmly Tier II. They'd have a lot of skills and Edges and be very, very, very good at Close Combat (especially with slashing weapons), but they're still basically human beings. They're not faster, stronger, smarter, etc than human beings can get. In many ways a regular Talent could outclass them. My I'm not remembering completely, but as I recall it, Immortals had three basic &quot;supernatural&quot; aspect. They were Immortal (no aging, only killed by decapitation). They could sense each within a (fairly small) areas. When one of them was killed and another was close enough, that other could absorb... energy/XP while it was present as some kind of weird electrical discharge.<br /> <br /> And that's it. Everything else about Immortals would be skills/edges/contacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T10:53:11-08:00","id":1349889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349876#post1349876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of power/Tier, based on my observations, Immortals are pretty firmly Tier II. They'd have a lot of skills and Edges and be very, very, very good at Close Combat (especially with slashing weapons), but they're still basically human beings. They're not faster, stronger, smarter, etc than human beings can get. In many ways a regular Talent could outclass them. My I'm not remembering completely, but as I recall it, Immortals had three basic &quot;supernatural&quot; aspect. They were Immortal (no aging, only killed by decapitation). They could sense each within a (fairly small) areas. When one of them was killed and another was close enough, that other could absorb... energy/XP while it was present as some kind of weird electrical discharge.<br /> <br /> And that's it. Everything else about Immortals would be skills/edges/contacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure there was an episode where Duncan fought someone in a stadium of some kind and they fell/jumped a significant distance from one level of seating down to the next without difficulty. I think at least one may have landed on their feet. Cassandra had clairvoyance, telepathy, and possibly other abilities. Kanis could at least partially control dogs (bragging he could get his dog to kill a kid with a thought), and Duncan seemed to get that ability after killing him.<br /> <br /> If you pull from the first movie, Immortals can also learn to breathe underwater and run as fast as horses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T13:38:36-08:00","id":1349906,"title":"","content":"They don\u2019t breath underwater, they just don\u2019t need to breath to live (they also don\u2019t need to eat, yet they usually do, and don\u2019t need any of their organs except for the connection brain-body working, but they help).<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t watch all the series, but watched enough to notice that even the supernatural powers they have are really weak if you compare it to a Psion. Cassandra Cv and TP are far from the minimum of a Psion or Psiad as I recall, and the communication to dogs don\u2019t seam to be better than the way animals read body language. They are all powers a tier 2 character can handle, as there is no real scale on them.<br /> <br /> Honestly, Immortals don\u2019t seam to be close to any of the 3 inspired enough to start with. I would make them an variation of Talents that can get some weird gifts, and those gifts become available to be learned by the immortal that killed him (the power is absorbed at the time, but the killer need some time and experience to learn how to deal with it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 11-20-2019, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T14:24:44-08:00","id":1349917,"title":"","content":"On Immortals I was thinking on a low level to use something like Superiors, though I could see Talents being used with some modification. Unless its a straight up super game I wouldn't use Psiads or Novas as their powers are in no way equivalent to a secret power game. <br /> <br /> As an aside a great source for material of a historic nature in gaming is the Dark Eras books by the Onyx Path, them and maybe even Mummy the Curse. Though that setting is a bit darker then Trinity and the rules are also a bit different much of the setting material and storyteller advice are easily transferred over. <br /> <br /> As an aside, and this is more towards Talents then it is Immortals, but the whole non-linear nature of mummies is a perfect way to describe something like a time traveling band of heroes. (I think I might see about looking at Curse in the light of said idea, hehe)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T14:59:05-08:00","id":1349927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349917#post1349917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Immortals I was thinking on a low level to use something like Superiors, though I could see Talents being used with some modification. Unless its a straight up super game I wouldn't use Psiads or Novas as their powers are in no way equivalent to a secret power game.<br /> <br /> As an aside a great source for material of a historic nature in gaming is the Dark Eras books by the Onyx Path, them and maybe even Mummy the Curse. Though that setting is a bit darker then Trinity and the rules are also a bit different much of the setting material and storyteller advice are easily transferred over.<br /> <br /> As an aside, and this is more towards Talents then it is Immortals, but the whole non-linear nature of mummies is a perfect way to describe something like a time traveling band of heroes. (I think I might see about looking at Curse in the light of said idea, hehe)</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually you might think about going a bit further back and checking out the Old World of Darkness's Mummy: The Resurrection. A bit of detail on that here: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mummy:_The_Resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mummy:_The_Resurrection</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T15:05:14-08:00","id":1349928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349927#post1349927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually you might think about going a bit further back and checking out the Old World of Darkness's Mummy: The Resurrection. A bit of detail on that here: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mummy:_The_Resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mummy:_The_Resurrection</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I LOVE Mummy the Resurrection. Irs like my all time favorite. (To the point I was, and sort of still am, mad that Mummy the Curse threw out its themes.) So yeah anything that uses it would be awesome. <br /> <br /> That said, how would this fit more an Immortal game then other ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T10:48:17-08:00","id":1350057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1349906#post1349906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, Immortals don\u2019t seam to be close to any of the 3 inspired enough to start with. I would make them an variation of Talents that can get some weird gifts, and those gifts become available to be learned by the immortal that killed him (the power is absorbed at the time, but the killer need some time and experience to learn how to deal with it).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Really it started as a joke explanation for why you don't have 5000 yearold Novas running around in game(Or psiads). Highlander gatherings clean up every Era with the last Nova/psiad hitting Q/P 10 and transcending.<br /> <br /> Then I noticed that Highlander Immortals kind work in the Continuum setup. Then there's always been desires to see more Flux Templates. We know of say at least 3 Quantum(Superior, Stalwart, Nova), Threeish Psi(Mesmerist, Psiad, Psion), but we don't seem to have even a second Flux Template aside from Mercer who we really don't get anything for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T12:49:33-08:00","id":1350086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1350057#post1350057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I noticed that Highlander Immortals kind work in the Continuum setup. Then there's always been desires to see more Flux Templates. We know of say at least 3 Quantum(Superior, Stalwart, Nova), Threeish Psi(Mesmerist, Psiad, Psion), but we don't seem to have even a second Flux Template aside from Mercer who we really don't get anything for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would make more than one Talent variation, one for Wuxia stile heroes, one Timelords stile and at least one in the immortals stile. The first 2 would be able to reach tier 3 (Psion stile) while the immortal would be a variation of a Talent. <br /> <br /> And for sure Immortals fit on TC, more than that, the rules are pretty much covered, only a few details that came in the series are out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T13:18:58-08:00","id":1350095,"title":"","content":"My argument for Immortals being Talents/paramorphs: If pulling a katana out from underneath your sauna towel isn't dramatic editing, I don't know what is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T14:31:06-08:00","id":1350127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1350095#post1350095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My argument for Immortals being Talents/paramorphs: If pulling a katana out from underneath your sauna towel isn't dramatic editing, I don't know what is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I laughed soo hard on this one I almost pee myself. Probably overreacted, but that\u2019s the true and it\u2019s funny...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T04:54:30-08:00","id":1350209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1350127#post1350127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I laughed soo hard on this one I almost pee myself. Probably overreacted, but that\u2019s the true and it\u2019s funny...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The sauna towel was the one that made me yell, &quot;REALLY?!?!?!&quot; at the screen. I could suspend disbelief with trenchcoats, but only a towel around your waist, I can't handle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T12:02:29-08:00","id":1350279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1350209#post1350209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The sauna towel was the one that made me yell, &quot;REALLY?!?!?!&quot; at the screen. I could suspend disbelief with trenchcoats, but only a towel around your waist, I can't handle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. This happened in an episode. I need to see it. Because that's EPIC! Do you know at least which season, if not the episode itself? hehe<br /> <br /> But yeah, that is some high level dramatic editing slash power use right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T12:18:39-08:00","id":1350284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1350279#post1350279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait. This happened in an episode. I need to see it. Because that's EPIC! Do you know at least which season, if not the episode itself? hehe<br /> <br /> But yeah, that is some high level dramatic editing slash power use right there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I want to say it's the season where mortals are killing immortals on holy ground. I'm relatively certain it is set in Paris. I'm pretty sure he follows the guy out of the sauna asking him if he speaks English, then switches to German, and then switches to French. (Although looking through IMDB, it might be the two-parter called Counterfeit in season 2 if it's the Tessa look-a-like he's following.) It might also be one of the post season 1 episodes with James Horton in it. Sorry my memory is so sketchy on this. I KNOW it happens, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T12:24:29-08:00","id":1350286,"title":"","content":"Highlander is basically just a serious implementation of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hammerspace\" target=\"_blank\">hammerspace</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T19:20:27-08:00","id":1350949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1340817-immortals-in-trinity-continuum?p=1350286#post1350286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Highlander is basically just a serious implementation of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hammerspace\" target=\"_blank\">hammerspace</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The best take I saw of that came in the Garth Ennis comic, Hitman. Due to some mad science, a guy ended up with tesseract technology effectively within his body as long as he could use the appropriate... orifice. Yes, this guys was able to literally pull guns, knives, even, with some visible straining, an entire sports car out of his ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","user":"johntfs","date":". 11-26-2019, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T00:59:24-08:00","id":1350992,"title":"","content":"Hitman have a bag similar of WoW bag, you can put a broken claw, a great sword or a armoured tiger in the same bag and they occupy the same space.<br /> <br /> Ok, not a single Broken claw, up to 5 of them...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}